{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791293534,"nonce":"JWmkFBXZmCXen6esDlnET2Zsht8=","title":"HIR heap scalarization loses allocation roots behind lossless pointer casts","message":"Pointer phis carrying local immutable allocations are scalarized, but their incoming values must name the allocation directly. Lua shaped constructors return a pointer through PtrToInt/IntToPtr or pointer bitcasts, so the phi graph rejects the incoming allocation before the address-use analysis can see it.\n\nThe current Lua Mandelbrot hot HIR contains a phi of two such casted Complex allocations. Track identity pointer conversions when connecting allocation/phi roots, continue rejecting truncation, field offsets and escapes, and use the canonical root when creating field phis. Keep the existing initialization, aliasing and mutation checks.\n\nThe first seven alternating NUC runs show Mandelbrot kernel 86.543 to 49.506 ms and wall 135.257 to 94.686 ms, all checksums correct; LuaJIT remains 19.425 ms kernel. Other sampled kernels are mostly unchanged. Tokenize differs between binaries despite identical hot HIR; a same-binary disable control retains that difference, and a matching rebuild is being checked before attributing it to this transformation.","files":null}]}